doc Skip to the next iteration of the innermost loop: continue
  In a `while` loop, `continue` runs the `next` block (if any) and then
  checks the condition again; in `for` it advances the loop variable.

  ```
  for i = 1 to 10
    if i % 2 == 0
      continue
    end
    print i      // the odd numbers
  end
  ```

  Only allowed inside a loop.

syntax statement inloop
  continue
